{
  "branches": ["main", "master"],
  "plugins": [
    "@semantic-release/commit-analyzer",
    "@semantic-release/release-notes-generator",
    "@semantic-release/changelog",
    [
      "@semantic-release/exec",
      {
        "prepareCmd": "sed -i 's/Version: .*/Version: ${nextRelease.version}/g' channel-sync-for-homey.php && sed -i 's/Stable tag: .*/Stable tag: ${nextRelease.version}/g' readme.txt && npm version ${nextRelease.version} --no-git-tag-version && sed -i 's/\"version\": \".*\"/\"version\": \"${nextRelease.version}\"/g' composer.json && sed -i 's/version-[0-9]*\\.[0-9]*\\.[0-9]*/version-${nextRelease.version}/g' README.md"
      }
    ],
    [
      "@semantic-release/git",
      {
        "assets": [
          "channel-sync-for-homey.php",
          "readme.txt",
          "package.json",
          "package-lock.json",
          "composer.json",
          "CHANGELOG.md",
          "README.md"
        ],
        "message": "chore(release): ${nextRelease.version} [skip ci]\n\n${nextRelease.notes}"
      }
    ],
    "@semantic-release/github"
  ]
}


---

### 2. Clean `README.md` Badge Setup

Replace the badge markup in your `README.md` with these two dynamic endpoints so they always reflect the latest release without caching mismatched versions:

```markdown
<!-- Single unified version badge pointing directly to GitHub Release -->
[![GitHub Release](https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/ejames17/channel-sync-for-homey?label=release&color=blue)](https://github.com/ejames17/channel-sync-for-homey/releases/latest)

<!-- WordPress Core / Tested Compatibility Badge -->
[![WordPress Tested](https://img.shields.io/badge/wordpress-6.0%2B-brightgreen)](https://wordpress.org)